{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA257311","title":"Hetrotrophic bacterial community assembly in two pilot and eight full-scale activated sludge wastewater treatment plants","description":"Abstract: Heterotrophic bacterial community assemblies at eight full-scale and two pilot scale activated sludge wastewater treatment plants (AS-WWTPs) were determined by high-throughput pyrosequencing of 16S rRNA gene amplicons. A total of 39 samples covered a range of abiotic factors spread over space and time (referred to as environmental gradients) and obtained over a period of 4 years.  The impact of environmental gradients on the community assemblies in AS-WWTPs, partitioned with respect to distances in position on the ecological gradients. Following gradients were considered specifically,: • Influent wastewater characteristics, • Seasonal variations (winter vs. summer) • Treatment process differences (conventional, oxidation ditch, and sequence batch reactor [SBR]) • Reactor sizes (pilot-scale vs. full-scale reactors) • Chemical stresses defined by a higher mortality induced by return activated sludge (RAS) ozonation (RAS-ozonated vs. non-ozonated reactors) • Inter-annual variation and geographical locations.","center":"McGill University","data_type":"Metagenome","submission_date":"2014/08/01 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN02950679","MIMS Environmental/Metagenome sample from wastewater metagenome","confirmed_urban","municipal_wastewater",null,null,"CA","Quebec",6077243,"Montréal","verified",45.43,-73.16,"Canada:Montreal",null,"populated place","wastewater treatment plant","Sewage","named urban infrastructure at sample level"],["SAMN02950680","MIMS Environmental/Metagenome sample from wastewater metagenome","confirmed_urban","muni